      14.227672576904297,
      14.308287620544434,
      14.331738471984863
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 2,
    "bbox": [
      63.49,
      504.08,
      537.05,
      586.97
    ],
    "text": "at about 6.30-7.00 she saw the accused-appellant passing her house and going down the lane. She has further said that she felt that he carried something in his hand but could not make out what it was. But she has clearly stated that she saw the accused-appellant and was able to",
    "fonts": [
      "Helvetica"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      13.814671516418457,
      13.890067100524902,
      13.971511840820312,
      14.120124816894531,
      14.162500381469727,
      14.199199676513672,
      14.199999809265137,
      14.224827766418457,
      14.226923942565918,
      14.227672576904297,
      14.269529342651367,
      14.293392181396484,
      14.309477806091309,
      14.331738471984863,
      14.462621688842773,
      14.641098976135254
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 2,
    "bbox": [
      64.53,
      588.57,
      537.16,
      608.08
    ],
    "text": "recognize him and also recognized him from his voice. She very clearly",
    "fonts": [
      "Helvetica"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      13.814671516418457,
      14.089167594909668,
      14.199999809265137
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 2,
    "bbox": [
      63.95,
      609.92,
      537.68,
      713.2
    ],
    "text": "stated to court that the accused-appellant passed her house around 6.30-700 p.m and went down the lane stating \"Killed Patta- do not give evidence.\" The accused-appellant is well known to the said two witnesses. There is no doubt that they have clearly recognized the accused -appellant as the person who stated that he had killed patta and",
    "fonts": [
      "Helvetica"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      13.456114768981934,
      13.580537796020508,
      14.162500381469727,
      14.179534912109375,
      14.187745094299316,
      14.199999809265137,
      14.203399658203125,
      14.22153377532959,
      14.224827766418457,
      14.227672576904297,
      14.246723175048828,
      14.265847206115723,
      14.292201042175293,
      14.39732837677002,
      14.45412540435791,
      14.4979248046875,
      14.631542205810547
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 3,
    "bbox": [
      64.04,
      71.23,
      537.16,
      132.86
    ],
    "text": "not to give evidence. In my view the two witnesses Karunaratne and Malini had clearly identified the accused -appellant as the person who uttered the words Ikilled Patta- do not give evidence\" beyond reasonable",
    "fonts": [
      "Helvetica"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      13.408650398254395,
      13.99304485321045,
      14.100000381469727,
      14.174653053283691,
      14.17748737335205,
      14.24178695678711,
      14.403141975402832,
      14.446785926818848
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 3,
    "bbox": [
      63.71,
      134.84,
      109.9,
      154.22
    ],
    "text": "doubt.",
    "fonts": [
      "Helvetica"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      14.100000381469727
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 3,
    "bbox": [
      63.79,
      164.11,
      537.46,
      183.49
    ],
    "text": "Witness Karunaratne has stated that the accused-appellant and the",
    "fonts": [
      "Helvetica"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      13.922229766845703,
      14.100000381469727,
      14.17748737335205,
      14.215526580810547
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 3,
    "bbox": [
      63.54,
      185.48,
      537.57,
      247.1
    ],
    "text": "deceased were not in good terms. There had been a quarrel between them about 7-8 months prior to the said incident. The wife of the deceased witness Srima Damayanthi too has testified to the fact that",
    "fonts": [
      "Helvetica"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      13.922229766845703,
      14.100000381469727,
      14.174653053283691,
      14.215526580810547,
      14.257817268371582,
      14.446785926818848,
      14.69446849822998
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 3,
    "bbox": [
      63.53,
      249.07,
      536.63,
      268.45
    ],
    "text": "there was animosity between the deceased and the accused-appellant.",
    "fonts": [
      "Helvetica"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      14.100000381469727,
      14.17748737335205
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 3,
    "bbox": [
      63.77,
      270.43,
      537.81,
      353.17
    ],
    "text": "Both witnesses Karunartne and Malini had very specifically stated that the accused-appellant said that he has killed the deceased and not to give evidence. Witness Karunaratne has also seen the accused-appellant carrying an axe in his hand and coming from the direction from where",
    "fonts": [
      "Helvetica"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      13.922229766845703,
      13.997577667236328,
      14.05101490020752,
      14.083040237426758,
      14.100000381469727,
      14.116690635681152,
      14.17211627960205,
      14.176741600036621,
      14.17748737335205,
      14.215526580810547
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 3,
    "bbox": [
      63.77,
      355.15,
      378.12,
      374.53
    ],
    "text": "the deceased was found fallen with cut injuries.",
    "fonts": [
      "Helvetica"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      14.100000381469727,
      14.222270011901855
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 3,
    "bbox": [
      63.75,
      384.43,
      537.46,
      403.81
    ],
    "text": "The doctor who held the post mortem had referred to a cut injury above",
    "fonts": [
      "Helvetica"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      14.100000381469727,
      14.134608268737793,
      14.15130615234375,
      14.178929328918457,
      14.57993221282959
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 3,
    "bbox": [
      64.01,
      405.79,
      537.83,
      425.17
    ],
    "text": "the neck of the deceased. 7 cm in length, due to which the tissues of the",
    "fonts": [
      "Helvetica"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      14.063152313232422,
      14.100000381469727,
      14.17748737335205,
      14.288095474243164,
      14.446785926818848,
      14.69446849822998
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 3,
    "bbox": [
      64.77,
      426.91,
      536.83,
      446.29
    ],
    "text": "brain too were injured. The doctor has classified the said injuries as fatal",
    "fonts": [
      "Helvetica"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      13.281599044799805,
      14.00296688079834,
      14.100000381469727,
      14.257817268371582
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 3,
    "bbox": [
      64.24,
      448.28,
      537.49,
      488.78
    ],
    "text": "injuries and has stated in his evidence that a person who receives this type of injuries cannot survive even for one minute.",
    "fonts": [
      "Helvetica"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      13.922229766845703,
      14.05101490020752,
      14.100000381469727,
      14.134608268737793,
      14.2811861038208,
      14.3035306930542,
      14.560287475585938
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 3,
    "bbox": [
      64.88,
      498.68,
      537.82,
      539.17
    ],
    "text": "It is well settled law that when the conviction is solely based on circumstantial evidence prosecution must prove that no one else but the",
    "fonts": [
      "Helvetica"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      13.337904930114746,
      14.095749855041504,
      14.100000381469727,
      14.2811861038208,
      14.346545219421387
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 3,
    "bbox": [
      64.89,
      541.41,
      277.72,
      560.78
    ],
    "text": "accused committed the offence.",
    "fonts": [
      "Helvetica"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      14.100000381469727
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 3,
    "bbox": [
      64.73,
      570.43,
      539.41,
      632.05
    ],
    "text": "In Podisinghe V. King 53 N.L.R49, it was held that in the case of circumstantial evidence it is the duty of the trial Judge to tell the Jury that such evidence must be totally inconsistent with the innocence of the",
    "fonts": [
      "Helvetica"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      13.337904930114746,
      13.541905403137207,
      13.829352378845215,
      13.854055404663086,
      14.005534172058105,
      14.05101490020752,
      14.05367374420166,
      14.09939956665039,
      14.100000381469727,
      14.160868644714355,
      14.17748737335205,
      14.215526580810547,
      14.222270011901855,
      14.223806381225586,
      14.288095474243164,
      14.346545219421387,
      14.446785926818848,
      14.560287475585938,
      14.589454650878906
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 3,
    "bbox": [
      65.37,
      633.79,
      399.27,
      653.17
    ],
    "text": "accused and must only be consistent with his guilt.",
    "fonts": [
      "Helvetica"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      14.05367374420166,
      14.100000381469727,
      14.222270011901855
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 3,
    "bbox": [
      64.97,
      662.6,
      539.99,
      703.09
    ],
    "text": "In Don Sunny V. The Attorney General 1998 (2) S.L.R 1, it was held that the charges sought to be proved by circumstantial evidence the items of",
    "fonts": [
      "Helvetica"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      13.3696870803833,
      13.541905403137207,
      13.630431175231934,
      13.938019752502441,
      13.99304485321045,
      14.07628059387207,
      14.100000381469727,
      14.17748737335205,
      14.215526580810547,
      14.424858093261719,
      14.446785926818848,
      14.589454650878906
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 4,
    "bbox": [
      59.6,
      72.2,
      533.0,
      91.58
    ],
    "text": "circumstantial evidence when taken together must irresistibly point",
    "fonts": [
      "Helvetica"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      14.100000381469727
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 4,
    "bbox": [
      59.23,
      93.55,
      507.89,
      112.93
    ],
    "text": "towards the only inference that the accused committed the offence.",
    "fonts": [
      "Helvetica"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      14.100000381469727,
      14.17748737335205,
      14.257817268371582,
      14.346545219421387
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 4,
    "bbox": [
      59.19,
      122.59,
      533.27,
      141.97
    ],
    "text": "The fact that the accused had the opportunity to commit the said murder",
    "fonts": [
      "Helvetica"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      14.07933521270752,
      14.100000381469727,
      14.167289733886719,
      14.17748737335205,
      14.195775032043457,
      14.2811861038208,
      14.312399864196777
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 4,
    "bbox": [
      59.99,
      143.96,
      532.05,
      163.34
    ],
    "text": "is not sufficient. The prosecution must prove that the act was done by",
    "fonts": [
      "Helvetica"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      13.337904930114746,
      14.100000381469727,
      14.174653053283691,
      14.17748737335205,
      14.2811861038208
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 4,
    "bbox": [
      59.44,
      165.32,
      532.3,
      205.82
    ],
    "text": "the accused alone and must exclude the possibility of the act done by some other person. In the case of The Queen V. Kularatne 71 N.L.R N.L.R",
    "fonts": [
      "Helvetica"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      13.403024673461914,
      13.790605545043945,
      13.84234619140625,
      13.915239334106445,
      13.99304485321045,
      14.100000381469727,
      14.131914138793945,
      14.17748737335205,
      14.257817268371582,
      14.560287475585938
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 4,
    "bbox": [
      59.59,
      207.79,
      533.99,
      248.29
    ],
    "text": "534, the Court of Criminal Appeal quoted with approval the dictum of Whitemeyer, J. in Rex V. Blom as follows:-",
    "fonts": [
      "Helvetica"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      12.548726081848145,
      13.408650398254395,
      13.541905403137207,
      13.61185073852539,
      14.05101490020752,
      14.100000381469727,
      14.17748737335205,
      14.222270011901855,
      14.424858093261719,
      14.560287475585938
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 4,
    "bbox": [
      59.44,
      257.96,
      531.64,
      298.46
    ],
    "text": "\"Two cardinal rules of logic governs the use of circumstantial evidence in the criminal trial:-",
    "fonts": [
      "Helvetica"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      14.004325866699219,
      14.100000381469727,
      14.424858093261719
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 4,
    "bbox": [
      60.12,
      308.59,
      505.9,
      327.97
    ],
    "text": "{1}The inference sought to be drawn must be consistent with all the",
    "fonts": [
      "Helvetica"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      13.938019752502441,
      14.05367374420166,
      14.100000381469727,
      14.222270011901855,
      14.446785926818848
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 4,
    "bbox": [
      77.53,
      338.12,
      516.77,
      357.5
    ],
    "text": "Approved facts. If it does not, then the inference cannot be drawn.",
    "fonts": [
      "Helvetica"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      14.05367374420166,
      14.100000381469727,
      14.17748737335205,
      14.260239601135254,
      14.359707832336426
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 4,
    "bbox": [
      60.61,
      367.16,
      529.8,
      386.54
    ],
    "text": "{2}The proof of facts should be such that they exclude every reasonable",
    "fonts": [
      "Helvetica"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      14.05367374420166,
      14.100000381469727,
      14.163108825683594,
      14.346545219421387,
      14.424858093261719
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 4,
    "bbox": [
      78.33,
      396.44,
      495.37,
      415.82
    ],
    "text": "Inference from them, save the one to be drawn. If they had not",
    "fonts": [
      "Helvetica"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      14.05367374420166,
      14.100000381469727,
      14.116690635681152,
      14.196917533874512,
      14.256828308105469,
      14.260239601135254,
      14.446785926818848
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 4,
    "bbox": [
      78.33,
      425.95,
      533.95,
      445.33
    ],
    "text": "excluded the other reasonable inferences, then there must be a doubt",
    "fonts": [
      "Helvetica"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      14.05367374420166,
      14.100000381469727,
      14.153299331665039,
      14.17748737335205,
      14.180569648742676
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 4,
    "bbox": [
      78.23,
      455.23,
      433.4,
      474.61
    ],
    "text": "whether the inference sought to be drawn is correct.\"",
    "fonts": [
      "Helvetica"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      13.337904930114746,
      13.938019752502441,
      14.100000381469727,
      14.119935989379883,
      14.17748737335205,
      14.446785926818848
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 4,
    "bbox": [
      60.15,
      484.51,
      533.26,
      525.01
    ],
    "text": "There is no direct evidence in this case. The items of evidence relied by the prosecution is purely circumstantial. Consideration of circumstantial",
    "fonts": [
      "Helvetica"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      13.532635688781738,
      14.031885147094727,
      14.100000381469727,
      14.560287475585938
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 4,
    "bbox": [
      60.81,
      526.99,
      532.31,
      546.37
    ],
    "text": "evidence has been vividly described by Pollock C.B. in Regina V. Exall",
    "fonts": [
      "Helvetica"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      13.403024673461914,
      13.536176681518555,
      13.936957359313965,
      14.00296688079834,
      14.091497421264648,
      14.100000381469727
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 4,
    "bbox": [
      61.4,
      547.14,
      532.84,
      567.28
    ],
    "text": "[1866] 4 F & F 922 at page 929, cited in King V. Guneratne [1946] 47 N.L.R",
    "fonts": [
      "Helvetica",
      "Times-Roman"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      13.541905403137207,
      13.790605545043945,
      14.09939956665039,
      14.100000381469727,
      15.100000381469727
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 4,
    "bbox": [
      61.22,
      569.23,
      322.35,
      588.61
    ],
    "text": "145 at page 149 in the following words:-",
    "fonts": [
      "Helvetica"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      14.100000381469727
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 4,
    "bbox": [
      60.8,
      598.27,
      535.43,
      638.77
    ],
    "text": "\"It has been said that circumstantial evidence is to be considered as a chain, and each piece as a link in the chain, but that is not so, for then, if",
    "fonts": [
      "Helvetica"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      13.140289306640625,
      13.281599044799805,
      13.337904930114746,
      13.922229766845703,
      14.05101490020752,
      14.100000381469727,
      14.13226318359375,
      14.17748737335205,
      14.215526580810547,
      14.256828308105469,
      14.3035306930542,
      14.346545219421387,
      14.512563705444336,
      14.57993221282959,
      14.589454650878906
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 4,
    "bbox": [
      60.89,
      640.75,
      535.43,
      722.78
    ],
    "text": "anyone link breaks, the chain would fall. It is more like the case of a rope comprised of several chords. One strand of the rope might be insufficient to sustain the weight, but three strands together may be quire of sufficient strength. Thus it may be in circumstantial evidence- there may",
    "fonts": [
      "Helvetica"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      13.337904930114746,
      13.915239334106445,
      14.05367374420166,
      14.100000381469727,
      14.133859634399414,
      14.17748737335205,
      14.312399864196777,
      14.359707832336426,
      14.424858093261719,
      14.560287475585938
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 5,
    "bbox": [
      64.05,
      71.96,
      537.45,
      91.34
    ],
    "text": "be a combination of circumstances, no one of which would raise a",
    "fonts": [
      "Helvetica"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      14.05367374420166,
      14.100000381469727,
      14.560287475585938
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 5,
    "bbox": [
      63.28,
      93.31,
      537.3,
      133.81
    ],
    "text": "reasonable conviction or more than a mere suspicion; but the three taken together may create a conclusion of guilt with as much certainty",
    "fonts": [
      "Helvetica"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      13.408650398254395,
      14.100000381469727,
      14.109196662902832,
      14.13226318359375,
      14.222270011901855,
      14.560287475585938
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 5,
    "bbox": [
      63.71,
      135.79,
      322.88,
      155.17
    ],
    "text": "as human affairs can require or admit.\"",
    "fonts": [
      "Helvetica"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      13.281599044799805,
      13.963540077209473,
      14.100000381469727,
      14.139195442199707,
      14.239212989807129
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 5,
    "bbox": [
      63.27,
      164.84,
      536.74,
      184.22
    ],
    "text": "The items of circumstantial evidence referred to earlier in this case in my",
    "fonts": [
      "Helvetica"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      13.915239334106445,
      14.100000381469727,
      14.446785926818848,
      14.560287475585938
    ]
  },
  {
